critique.notes:
The direction is sound and covers most of the prior critique's required changes 1-6:
- first-open txs are indexed per transaction;
- the walk is worker-owned and does not wait on the UI;
- the state row is written in the same transaction as the truncate;
- every slice consumes at least one datom and the commit counts against the budget;
- no db value is held across a yield.

The AEVT walk from (inc cursor) with the `(not= :block/uuid (:a dt))` stop is correct for the fork's seek-datoms, which runs to the end of the index.

The main gaps are:
- whether 'complete' can be trusted (crash or swallowed errors);
- heal semantics (stale rows, and a full-db restore for every upgraded user);
- one real bug: the cursor is persisted as a string;
- the reset-conn! hook runs in the wrong place.

